  "answer": "Both files are correct. Let me summarize the changes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented route resolution in the request entry point by editing two writable files.\n\n### `entry.mjs` — production entry point\n`dispatch(path)` now delegates directly to `resolveFromRegistry(path, defaultRoutes)`, using the fixture's default routes as the production route table. It no longer consults `legacyResolve`, so the legacy `/old/help` behavior is no longer part of the production entry point.\n\n### `registry.mjs` — lower-level resolver\nRewrote `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)` to implement the required matching policy. The previous version had two bugs: it returned a fallback as soon as it encountered one (even if a later static/dynamic route matched), and it returned the first matching dynamic route before considering a later static route.\n\nThe new implementation:\n- **Validates** the path up front, throwing `TypeError` for non-strings, empty strings, or strings not beginning with `/`.\n- **Scans all records once**, returning immediately on the first matching **static** record (so any static match beats any dynamic match regardless of declaration order, and the first declared static wins).\n- **Remembers the first matching dynamic** record only if none has been recorded yet (first matching dynamic wins).\n- **Remembers the first fallback** record only if none has been recorded yet.\n- After the scan, returns the dynamic match if present, otherwise the fallback, otherwise `null`.\n- **Never mutates records** and returns fresh plain objects (`params` objects come from `matchDynamic`/`fallbackResult`, and static matches build a new `{ route, params: {} }`).\n\nMatching remains case-sensitive and trailing-slash-distinct because `matchStatic` uses strict equality and `matchDynamic` splits on `/` and compares literal segments exactly, requiring nonempty dynamic segments.\n\n### Untouched files\n`legacy.mjs` (and its `/old/help` behavior), the adapters, and the path/query/header utilities were left unchanged, as required. The existing tests in `public.test.mjs` align with the new behavior (static-before-dynamic ordering, dynamic params, fallback, adapter reuse, and empty-registry `null`).",
